 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S442-018\", \"clauses\": {\"count\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F04\", \"template\": \"Count by halves: 1/2, ___. What fraction comes next?\", \"reasoning\": \"F04 is a counting-by-halves sequence with a blank to fill, built on the task clause Count. Its denominator and operation are chosen from the lc's declared bounds (unit_fraction, count_sequence).\"}, \"halves\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F09\", \"template\": \"What comes next when counting by halves: 1/2, ___?\", \"reasoning\": \"F09 names halves as the object being counted. The word halves is in curriculum_vocab.\"}, \"quarters\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"Count by quarters: 1/4, 2/4, 3/4, ___. What fraction comes next?\", \"reasoning\": \"F05 counts quarters in a unit-fraction sequence. The word quarters is in curriculum_vocab.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F07\", \"F12\", \"F15\", \"F18\", \"F19\", \"F21\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Put the result over the same {den_lbl}: {step}/{den}.\", \"What fraction is missing when counting by quarters: {join}?\", \"When {verb} {frac_lbl}s with the same {den_lbl}, keep the {den_lbl} the same.\", \"{p0}, {p1}, {p2}, {p3}\", \"{replace} only the {num_lbl}s: {a_num} {sign} {b_num} = {step}.\", \"{member}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F15 and F07 teach adding and subtracting fractions that share a bottom number. The lc says only Count halves and quarters, and the declared operation is count_sequence alone, so this is an operation beyond scope. F19 pairs an Add or Subtract verb with a + or - sign drawn from separate domains with no link between them, so a learner can be told to add with a minus sign. Its b_num domain is printed only as 0. F21 members include 4/3, which is thirds and outside halves and quarters, and also 1/2, 3/2 and 4/2 alongside quarter members. F18 joins F17 and F21 values with no denominator constraint, and F12 nests F18 under a count-by